<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{title}}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header" id="top">
      <p class="brand">{{name}}</p>
      <nav aria-label="Site sections">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#sec-1">{{sections.0}}</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sec-2">{{sections.1}}</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sec-3">{{sections.2}}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <h1>{{name}}</h1>
      <p>{{who}}</p>
      <p><a class="button" href="#inquiry">{{mainAction.label}}</a></p>

      <section id="sec-1">
        <h2>{{sections.0}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-2">
        <h2>{{sections.1}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-3">
        <h2>{{sections.2}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="offer">
        <h2>What we offer</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          {{#each items}}<article class="card">
            <h3>{{title}}</h3>
            <p>{{text}}</p>
            <p class="price">{{price}}</p>
          </article>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="inquiry">
        <h2>{{mainAction.label}}</h2>
        <form action="/inquiry" method="post">
          <p>
            <label for="f-name">What should we call you?</label><br>
            <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
          </p>
          <p>
            <label for="f-phone">Phone</label><br>
            <input id="f-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required>
          </p>
          <p><button type="submit">{{mainAction.label}}</button></p>
        </form>
      </section>
    </main>


    <section data-scaffold id="language-choice">
      <h2>Choosing a server language</h2>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Language</th><th>Start-up speed</th><th>Run speed</th><th>Concurrency</th><th>Ecosystem</th><th>Hiring</th><th>Entry barrier</th><th>Total</th></tr>
        <tr class="lang"><td class="name">PHP</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">2</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="total">23</td></tr>
        <tr class="lang"><td class="name">Python (Django)</td><td class="score">4</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="total">25</td></tr>
        <tr class="lang"><td class="name">Go</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="score">5</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="score">3</td><td class="total">22</td></tr>
      </table>
      <p id="choice">Choice: PHP. The project has a section “{{sections.0}}”, pages of text and one inquiry form, so there is little dynamic content, there are no live connections, and above all hosting and specialists are ready. The speed of execution doesn’t decide anything here.</p>
      <p id="hiring">Specialists: PHP developers are easy to find through job boards and freelance communities, and a studio or an independent developer can set up WordPress for the project.</p>
      <p id="revisit">I’ll revisit the choice if long connections appear (a chat, live notifications) or a heavy flow of requests: then I’ll look at Go, Node.js or Elixir.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>{{name}}, {{city}}</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
`,
