			},
			checks: [
				{ id: 'choice-section', kind: 'exists', selector: '#language-choice' },
				{ id: 'no-blanks', kind: 'text', selector: '#language-choice', matches: '^[^…]*$' },
				{ id: 'three-languages', kind: 'count', selector: '#language-choice tr.lang', min: 3 },
				{ id: 'language-names', kind: 'text', selector: '#language-choice td.name', matches: 'PHP|Python|Ruby|Java|C#|Go|JavaScript|Node|Elixir|Rust|Kotlin' },
				{ id: 'scores', kind: 'text', selector: '#language-choice td.score', matches: '^\\s*[1-5]\\s*$' },
				{ id: 'totals', kind: 'text', selector: '#language-choice td.total', matches: '^\\s*\\d{1,2}\\s*$' },
				{ id: 'choice-reasoned', kind: 'text', selector: '#choice', matches: '^(?=[\\s\\S]*(?:PHP|Python|Ruby|Java|C#|Go|JavaScript|Node|Elixir|Rust|Kotlin))(?=[\\s\\S]*(?:because|since|so |which means|means))' },
				{ id: 'choice-uses-brief', kind: 'field', selector: '#choice', field: 'sections', min: 1 },
				{ id: 'hiring', kind: 'text', selector: '#hiring', matches: 'find|hire|hiring|job board|communit|freelanc|studio|recruit|vacanc|agenc' },
				{ id: 'revisit', kind: 'text', selector: '#revisit', matches: '^(?=[\\s\\S]*(?:if|when|once))(?=[\\s\\S]*\\S{4,})' }
			]
		},
		quiz: [
			{
				type: 'single',
				prompt: 'You need a business-card site and you choose WordPress. Which language comes “in the box”?',
				options: ['PHP', 'Rust', 'Elixir'],
				answer: 0,
				why: [
					'Yes. WordPress is written in PHP, like Drupal and Joomla. When you choose a content management system, you choose its language too.',
					'No: none of the popular systems for business-card sites is written in Rust.',
					'No: Elixir is chosen for other jobs, such as chats and event streams.'
				]
			},
			{
				type: 'match',
				prompt: 'Match each language with its typical niche',
				pairs: [
					['PHP', 'sites on content management systems, and cheap hosting'],
					['Python', 'fast development, data and neural networks, the Django framework'],
					['Go', 'simple fast services that take many requests at once'],
					['Elixir', 'chats and event streams: thousands of connections on one machine'],
					['Rust', 'places where extreme speed and memory safety matter']
				]
			},
			{
				type: 'multiple',
				prompt: 'What is worth weighing when you choose a language for a project?',
				options: [
					'What the project has to do (forms, a chat, calculations)',
					'Who you can hire, and how fast',
					'Where the project will live (which hosting supports the language)',
					'Which language is in the news right now'
				],
				answer: [0, 1, 2],
				why: [
					'Yes: the task sets the demands on speed, concurrency and the shape of the server.',
					'Yes: a language nobody can write will cost more than any other.',
					'Yes: cheap hosting often runs only PHP, and other languages need a server of their own.',
					'No: fashion passes quickly, and the project stays.'
				]
			},
			{
				type: 'single',
				prompt: 'Rust is faster than PHP. Why does almost nobody choose it for a business-card site?',
				options: [
					'Speed of execution isn’t the bottleneck of a business card, while the high entry barrier and the lack of ready-made systems cost a lot',
					'Rust can’t work over a network',
					'Rust is banned on hosting services'
				],
				answer: 0,
				why: [
					'Yes. The bottleneck of an ordinary site is the network, the database and development, not the speed of the language. It doesn’t pay to buy speed you don’t need with extra complexity.',
					'No: it can, and fast network services are written in it.',
					'No: nothing bans it. It is just less often preinstalled on cheap hosting.'
				]
			},
			{
				type: 'single',
				prompt: 'How is the choice of Elixir for chats and notification systems explained?',
				options: [
					'It runs on the Erlang virtual machine, built for phone systems: a great many light parallel processes, and resilience to failures',
					'It is the most widespread language in the world',
					'It runs right in the browser'
				],
				answer: 0,
				why: [
					'Yes. Erlang was invented at Ericsson for phone exchanges, where millions of calls go on at once and must not be cut off. Elixir (2011) gives a modern language on top of the same machine.',
					'No: it is niche, and specialists are few, especially in some markets.',
					'No: what runs in the browser is JavaScript.'
				]
			},
			{
				type: 'single',
				prompt: 'What does “entry barrier” mean in a table where 5 is the best score?',
				options: [
					'5: easy to start, little knowledge and few tools needed at once',
					'5: the language is very hard',
					'5: the language is the fastest'
				],
				answer: 0,
				why: [
					'Yes. We agreed that a bigger number is always better for the project. For the entry barrier that means “low”, so it is easy to start.',
					'No: then a five would be a bad score, and in the table every criterion works the same way.',
					'No: speed of execution is a column of its own.'
				]
			}
		],
		cards: [
			{
				id: 'server-niche-php',
				front: 'Where does PHP live, and why?',
				back: 'Sites on content management systems: WordPress, Drupal, Laravel (and 1C-Bitrix in Russia). Cheap hosting, the “one request, one process” model, a huge ecosystem and many specialists. It is weaker where long connections are needed.'
			},
			{
				id: 'server-niche-python-ruby',
				front: 'What are Python and Ruby known for on the server?',
				back: 'Python (Django, Flask, FastAPI): fast development, data and neural networks. Ruby (Rails, 2004): speed in building products, “convention over configuration”. Both are slower than Go or Java, but enough for most sites.'
			},
			{
				id: 'server-niche-jvm',
				front: 'Where are Java and C# used?',
				back: 'Enterprise systems, banks, big portals. Strict typing, mature frameworks (Spring, .NET), many specialists. A high entry barrier and a heavy start for a project.'
			},
			{
				id: 'server-niche-go-node',
				front: 'What are Go and Node.js good for?',
				back: 'Go (Google, 2009): simplicity, speed, easy concurrency; Docker and Kubernetes are written in it. Node.js (2009): one language on the server and in the browser, the huge npm ecosystem, quick prototypes and live connections.'
			},
			{
				id: 'server-niche-elixir-rust',
				front: 'What are Elixir and Rust chosen for?',
				back: 'Elixir (on the Erlang VM): chats, event streams, resilience, but few specialists. Rust: top speed and memory safety for services where that matters, but a high entry barrier.'
			}
		],
		sources: [
